From b3e0be90e6a024474c3df9c9264d486be0408b10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:39:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix moving-GC sources and export heap-owned code literals

Mark DFS nodes before scanning self edges, refresh allocating string primitives, and copy pushed binary literals to heap ownership so live code compaction cannot invalidate VM roots. Bound primitive-name components and parse hexadecimal/binary values with explicit overflow checks independent of ILP32 long saturation. Verified shared baseline and 385 GC regressions on LP64 ASan/UBSan, legacy 32-bit UBSan under qemu-i386, and RV64 emulator.

Co-authored-by: Shelley <shelley@exe.dev>
---
 vm/PORTABILITY.md | 15 ++++++++++-----
 vm/dataPrims.c    | 21 ++++-----------------
 vm/interp.c       | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 vm/mem.c          |  4 ++++
 vm/miscPrims.c    | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 vm/runtime.c      |  4 ++--
 6 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vm/PORTABILITY.md b/vm/PORTABILITY.md
index 23a48fa..8092642 100644
--- a/vm/PORTABILITY.md
+++ b/vm/PORTABILITY.md
@@ -48,8 +48,13 @@ needed, and this profile does not require libm or mbFont. Hardware reset uses
 hooks and the interpreter's hardwired I/O entry points still need a backend;
 unsupported user operations should report `primitiveNotImplemented`.
 
-Heap GC forwards all VM roots and references. It does not relocate live
-references into a moving code store. Code-store compaction therefore still
-requires stopping tasks and clearing literal-bearing live state on platforms
-that move code; this port does not claim arbitrary live-update relocation or
-power-loss-safe persistence.
+`pushLiteral` copies packed string/byte-array literals into the heap before
+exporting them to the VM stack. Globals, lists, task stacks, and broadcast
+roots therefore never retain language-visible references into the moving code
+store. Lookup-only primitive-name operands still refer directly to code and
+are not exported. Native suspended-task code pointers are repaired by chunk
+index after code compaction; saved IPs and return addresses are offsets.
+Changing the contents of a currently executing chunk still needs the caller's
+usual stop/update policy; this port does not claim arbitrary live-update
+replacement or power-loss-safe persistence. Native extensions must not bypass
+this ownership policy by retaining code-store handles.
